{"r":"Hdb","lane":{"p":527,"e":[{"h":"حَدِبَ","t":["aor , inf. n. ",[2,"حَدَبٌ"],"; (S, * A, Mgh, * Msb, K;) and ↓ ",[2,"احدبّ"],", and ↓ ",[2,"تحادب"],", (K,) and ↓ ",[2,"احدودب"],"; (S, K;) ",[1,"He"]," (a man, Msb) ",[1,"was,"]," or ",[1,"became, humpbaked;"]," (Mgh, Msb;) ",[1,"he had a prominent,"]," or ",[1,"protuberant, back, and a hollow,"]," or ",[1,"receding, chest"]," (A, * K) ",[1,"and belly:"]," (K:) [accord. to the Msb, from ",[2,"حَدَبٌ"]," signifying “ elevated ground; ” but the reverse is indicated in the A:] and ",[1,"it"]," (the back) ",[1,"was,"]," or ",[1,"became, humped,"]," or ",[1,"protuberant;"]," (S, A; *) as also ↓ ",[2,"انحدب"],". (KL.) ― -b2- And the first, (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"It"]," (a thing) ",[1,"rose,"]," or ",[1,"grew up"]," or ",[1,"out, high:"]," (KL:) [",[1,"it was,"]," or ",[1,"became, gibbous,"]," or ",[1,"convex;"]," as also ↓ ",[2,"احدودب"],".] ― -b3- ",[2,"حَدِبَ عَليْهِ"],", (S, A, K,) inf. n. as above; (KL, TA;) and ↓ ",[2,"تحدّب"],"; (S, A, K;) (tropical:) ",[1,"He was,"]," or ",[1,"became, affectionate, favourable,"]," or ",[1,"kind, to him."]," (S, A, * K, KL, TA.) And ",[2,"حَدِبَتْ عَلَى وَلَدِهَا"],", (K, * TA,) inf. n. as above; (TA;) and ↓ ",[2,"تحدّبت"],"; (K;) (tropical:) ",[1,"She"]," (a woman) ",[1,"applied herself constantly to the care of her child,"]," or ",[1,"children, after the loss of her husband, not marrying again."]," (K, TA.) -A2- ",[2,"حَدَبَ"],[2,"عَنْهُ"],", aor. , inf. n. ",[2,"حَدْبٌ"],", ",[1,"He repelled from him, and defended him."]," (MF, TA.)"],"f":"1"},{"h":"تَحْدِيبٌ","t":["[inf. n. of ",[2,"حدّب"],"] The act of ",[1,"elevating,"]," or ",[1,"raising high, the back."]," (KL.) ― -b2- [And, accord. to Golius, as on the authority of the KL, The ",[1,"making"]," a thing ",[1,"gibbous,"]," or ",[1,"convex:"]," but this meaning which the word has in the present day, I do not find in my copy of the KL.]"],"f":"2"},{"h":"احدبهُ","t":[[1,"He"]," (God) ",[1,"rendered him humpbacked."]," (S.) ― -b2- (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"He,"]," or ",[1,"it, rendered him affectionate, favourable,"]," or ",[1,"kind."]," (KL.)"],"f":"4"},{"h":"تَحَدَّبَ","t":["see 1, in two places. ― -b2- ",[2,"تحدّب بِهِ"],[1,"He,"]," or ",[1,"it, clung,"]," or ",[1,"clave, to it."]," (K, TA.)"],"f":"5"},{"h":"تَحَاْدَبَ","t":["see 1."],"f":"6"},{"h":"إِنْحَدَبَ","t":["see 1."],"f":"7"},{"h":"إِحْدَبَّ","t":["see 1."],"f":"9"},{"h":"إِحْدَوْدَبَ","t":["see 1, in two places. ― -b2- Also (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"It"]," (sand) ",[1,"was,"]," or ",[1,"became, curved,"]," or ",[1,"winding;"]," or ",[1,"curved,"]," or ",[1,"winding, and long."]," (K.)"],"f":"12"},{"h":"حَدَبٌ","t":["(tropical:) ",[1,"High,"]," or ",[1,"elevated, ground;"]," so in the Kur xxi. 96; (S, A, Msb;) as also ↓ ",[2,"حَدَبَةٌ"],"; and so ",[2,"حَدَبٌ مِنَ الأَرْضِ"],": (A:) or ",[1,"rugged and high ground:"]," (T, K:) pl. ",[2,"حِدَابٌ"]," (S) [and app., accord. to the TA, ",[2,"أَحْدَابٌ"]," also, a pl. of pauc.]. And ",[2,"حَدَبُ الرَّمْلِ"]," (tropical:) ",[1,"Sand brought by the wind,"]," [or ",[1,"blown together,"],"] ",[1,"and elevated."]," (A, TA.) And hence, as being likened to such sand, (IAar, TA,) ",[2,"حَدَبُ البُهْمَى"]," (tropical:) ",[1,"What is scattered, and heaped up, of"]," [",[1,"the species of barley-grass called"],"] ",[2,"بهمى"],". (IAar, K, TA.) And ",[2,"حَدَبُ المَآءِ"]," (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"The elevated waves of water:"]," (T, TA:) or ",[1,"the rolling over of water, volume over volume:"]," (K, TA:) or ",[1,"the rolling of water in waves."]," (TA.) And ",[2,"حَدَبُ الغَدِيرِ"]," (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"The motion and waves of the pool of water left by a torrent."]," (IAar, TA.) And ",[2,"حَدَبُ السَّيْل"]," (tropical:) ",[1,"The rise,"]," or ",[1,"swell, and abundance, of the torrent."]," (A, TA.) ― -b2- (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"A slope in a declivity;"]," expl. by ",[2,"حَدُورٌ فِى صَبَبٍ"],", as in the correct copies of the K, and in the L; in some copies of the K ",[2,"حدوب"],"; (TA;) [in the CK ",[2,"حُدُورٌ"],";] as the ",[2,"حَدَب"]," of waves (in some copies of the K, of the wind, TA, [an evident mistranscription, ",[2,"الريح"]," for ",[2,"الموج"],",]) and of sand. (K.) ― -b3- (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"A mark left upon the skin;"]," (As, K;) such as the [",[1,"weal"]," or] ",[1,"swelling and thickness produced by beating."]," (As, TA.) ― -b4- (tropical:) The ",[1,"intenseness of the cold"]," of winter. (A, K.) -A2- ",[1,"A certain plant:"]," or the [",[1,"plant called"],"] ",[2,"نَصِىّ"],". (K.)"]},{"h":"حَدِبٌ","t":[": see ",[2,"أَحْدَبُ"],". ― -b2- Also (tropical:) ",[1,"Affectionate, favourable,"]," or ",[1,"kind."]," (A, TA.) You say, ",[2,"هُوَ حَدِبٌ"],[2,"عَلَى أَخِيهِ"]," (tropical:) ",[1,"He is affectionate,"]," &c., ",[1,"to his brother."]," (A.) -A2- ",[2,"أَرْضٌ حَدِبَةٌ"],[1,"A land abounding with the plant called"],[2,"حَدَب"],". (K.)"]},{"h":"حَذَبَةٌ","t":[[1,"A hump on the back."]," (Az, S, A, Mgh.) ― -b2- See also ",[2,"حَدَبٌ"],"."]},{"h":"حَدَابِ","t":["like ",[2,"قَطَامِ"],", (K,) indecl., (TA,) (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"A year of drought, barrenness,"]," or ",[1,"dearth:"]," (K:) or ",[1,"a year of severe drought."]," (TA.)"]},{"h":"حُدَيْبَآءُ","t":[": see what next follows."]},{"h":"أَحْدَبُ","t":[[1,"Humpbacked;"]," (S, Mgh, Msb;) ",[1,"having a prominent,"]," or ",[1,"protuberant, back, and a hollow,"]," or ",[1,"receding, chest and belly;"]," (K;) and ↓ ",[2,"حَدِبٌ"]," signifies the same: (Sb, S, K:) fem. of the former ",[2,"حَدْبَآءُ"],": (Msb:) and pl. ",[2,"حُدْبٌ"],". (Msb, TA.) ",[2,"اِبْنَةٌ"]," ↓ ",[2,"حُدَيْبَآءُ"]," (dim. of ",[2,"حَدْبَآءُ"],"), meaning ",[1,"A little humpbacked daughter,"]," occurs in a trad. (TA.) ― -b2- Hence, ",[2,"آلَةٌ حَدْبَآءُ"],", (see a verse of Kaab Ibn-Zuheyr, voce ",[2,"آلَةٌ"],", in art. ",[2,"اول"],",) (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"A gibbous bier:"]," (A, * TA:) or (as used in that verse) it means ",[1,"a distressing state,"]," or ",[1,"condition:"]," or ",[1,"an elevated apparatus."]," (TA.) And ",[2,"رَمْلَةٌ حَدْبَآءُ"]," (assumed tropical:) [",[1,"A gibbous tract of sand"],"]. (ISh, K in art. ",[2,"دبح"],", &c.) And ",[2,"نَاقَةٌ"],[2,"حَدْبَآءُ"],", (S, A,) or ",[2,"دَابَّةٌ حدبَآءُ"],", (K,) (tropical:) ",[1,"A she-camel,"]," (S, A,) or ",[1,"a beast,"]," (K,) ",[1,"the prominent parts of whose hips,"]," (S, A, K,) ",[1,"and the bone of whose back,"]," (TA,) ",[1,"appear,"]," (S, A, K,) ",[1,"by reason of her leanness."]," (A, TA.) And ",[2,"حَدْبَآءُ حِدْبِيرٌ"]," and ",[2,"حِدْبَارٌ"]," are expressions used in the same sense: (L, TA:) pl. ",[2,"حُدْبٌ حَدَابِيرُ"],". (S, L, TA.) ― -b3- ",[2,"الأَحْدَبُ"]," is the name of ",[1,"A vein"]," (",[2,"عِرْق"],") ",[1,"penetrating into,"]," or ",[1,"lying within, the bone"]," (",[2,"عَظْمَ"]," [app. a mistranscription for ",[2,"عَظَمَة"]," the ",[1,"upper portion"],"]) ",[1,"of the fore-arm."]," (K.) ― -b4- ",[2,"أَمْرٌ أَحْدَبُ"]," (A) and ",[2,"خُطَّةٌ حَدْبَآءُ"]," (A, TA) (tropical:) ",[1,"A difficult affair:"]," (A, TA:) and ",[2,"أُمُورٌ حُدْبٌ"]," (A, TA) and ",[2,"حُدْبُ الأُمُورِ"]," (K) (tropical:) ",[1,"difficult affairs;"]," (A, K, TA;) sing. ",[2,"حَدْبَآءُ"]," [for ",[2,"خُطَّةٌ حَدْبَآءُ"]," or the like]. (K.) And ",[2,"سَنَةٌ حَدْبَآءُ"]," (tropical:) ",[1,"A severe, cold year."]," (A, TA.) [Hence,] ",[2,"وَسِيقٌ أَحْدَبُ"]," (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"A quick driving."]," (TA.) ― -b5- [Hence, also,] ",[2,"الأَحْدَبُ"]," [used as a subst.] (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"Vehemence, severity, difficulty,"]," or ",[1,"distress;"]," syn. ",[2,"الشِّدَّةُ"],". (K.) -A2- [Also (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"More,"]," and ",[1,"most, affectionate, favourable,"]," or ",[1,"kind."],"] ",[2,"أَحْدَبُهُمْ عَلَى"],[2,"المُسْلِمِينَ"],", said of Aboo-Bekr, in a trad. of 'Alee, means (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"The most affectionate, favourable,"]," or ",[1,"kind, of them, to the Muslims."]," (TA.)"]}]},"maqayis":["الحاء والدال والباء أصل واحد، وهو ارتفاع الشيء. فالحدب ما ارتفع من الأرض. قال الله تعالى: {وهم من كل حدب ينسلون} [الأنبياء: 96] . والحدب في الظهر ; يقال حدب واحدودب. وناقة حدباء، إذا بدت حراقفها ; وكذلك الحدبار. يقال هن حدب حدابير. فأما قولهم حدب عليه إذا عطف وأشفق، فهو من هذا، لأنه كأنه جنأ عليه من الإشفاق، وذلك شبيه بالحدب."],"mufradat":["يجوز أن يكون الأصل في الحدب حدب الظهر، يقال: حدب الرجل حدبا، فهو أحدب، واحدودب. وناقة حدباء تشبيها به، ثم شبه به ما ارتفع من ظهر الأرض، فسمي حدبا، قال تعالى: وهم من كل حدب ينسلون [الأنبياء/ 96] ."]}